{{also|Plateau}}
==English==
[[Image:Plateau (PSF).png|thumb|right|Diagram showing plateaus.]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|plateau|notext=1}}, diminutive of {{m|fr|plat||a plate}}; see {{m|en|plate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈplætəʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/plæˈtoʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-plateau.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* Homophones: [[plateaux#Pronunciation|plateaux]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|plateaus|plateaux}}

# A largely [[level]] [[expanse]] of [[land]] at a high [[elevation]]; [[tableland]].
# A comparatively [[stable]] level in something that [[varies]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} An [[ornamental]] [[dish]] for the table; a [[tray]] or [[salver]].
# {{lb|en|sports|broadcasting}} A notable level of attainment or achievement.

